6462	6601	Personal life
Bjerregaard grew up in Vesterbro in Copenhagen as the daughter of joiner Gudmund Bjerregaard and bookkeeper Rita Bjerregaard.
6602	6639	She was the oldest of three siblings.
6640	6758	She was hospitalized several times because of narrow and unhealthy conditions, until the family acquired an allotment.
6759	6902	She finished her exam from Christianshavn Gymnasium in 1958 and became a modern side student from Statens Kursus til Studentereksamen in 1966.

6902	7030	After getting her teachers' certificate in 1964 from Emdrupborg, she worked as a folkeskole (primary school) teacher until 1970.
7031	7102	In the same period she was a consultant for publishing house Gyldendal.
7103	7174	In 1971, she became assistant professor at Odense College of Education.
7175	7233	She has been married to historian Søren Mørch since 1966.

7233	7328	In her spare time, she was a gardener on her organically-managed manor, mostly growing apples.

7328	7446	Bjerregaard wrote several books during her life, latest being the first volume of her memoirs titled 'Ritt' (2015).



7446	7545	Death
Bjerregaard died of cancer at her home in Copenhagen on 21 January 2023, at the age of 81.



